# Citation metadata for pyALDIC-3D (Citation File Format 1.2.0).
# Maintainer notes:
# - `version` must be bumped together with src/al_dic_3d/__init__.py at every
#   release (see docs/RELEASING.md).
# - `date-released` and the Zenodo concept DOI are filled in at the FIRST public
#   release: Zenodo mints the DOI when the first GitHub Release is published
#   (do not invent a DOI before that).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use pyALDIC-3D in your research, please cite it using the metadata in
  this file, together with the method papers listed under `references`.
type: software
title: "pyALDIC-3D: stereo / 3D Digital Image Correlation built on the pyALDIC platform"
abstract: >-
  pyALDIC-3D is an independent, self-contained desktop application and headless
  CLI for stereo (two-camera) Digital Image Correlation. It reconstructs
  full-field 3D shape, displacement, and Green-Lagrange surface strain from
  synchronized stereo image sequences, using the Augmented-Lagrangian DIC engine
  of the pyALDIC 2D platform (al-dic) and following the MATLAB 3D-Stereo-ALDIC
  reference implementation as its mathematical model.
authors:
